  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 1248 PM MST Sun Nov 22 2026\n\nTransitory ridging builds across the region into Wednesday, \nleading to dry conditions and warming temperatures. Latest \noperational and ensemble model data coming into better agreement\nof more eastern Pacific energy splitting as it translates \nacross the Intermountain West Thursday and Friday. This will \nkeep the region in moderate northwest flow into the end of the \nThanksgiving Holiday weekend, with chances of precipitation \nconfined mainly to the Northern and Central Mtns, and \ntemperatures remaining at or slightly above seasonal levels. \nHowever, will need to continue to monitor the potential for \nsurface high pressure building across the Northern High Plains \nto send a backdoor cold front into eastern Colorado later next \nweekend.",
